Package: spbm-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, dkms (>= 2.1.0.0)
Recommends: linux-headers-nvidia-hwe-24.04 | linux-headers-generic | linux-headers
Description: hwmon driver for DGX Spark whole-system power telemetry
 Reads the System Power Budget Manager shared memory region that the MediaTek
 SSPM firmware maintains on the NVIDIA GB10 SoC, and exposes it through the
 standard hwmon sysfs interface.
 .
 This is the only way to read whole-system power on a DGX Spark. NVIDIA's
 nvidia-smi reports the GPU rail alone, which does not span even its own
 package: the GB10 SoC is rated at 140 W for CPU and GPU together inside a
 240 W system. The firmware measures the rest and keeps it in registers no
 shipped driver binds.
 .
 Fourteen power channels including total system input, four cumulative energy
 accumulators in millijoules, eight thermal zones, and writable power limits.
 .
 Built by DKMS against the running kernel, so it survives kernel upgrades. On
 a Secure Boot machine DKMS signs the module with the machine owner key and
 the installer will prompt you to enrol it, which needs a keyboard at the
 console once.
